s\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Verify build/install and update README\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Inspect CSV headers and representative rows","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Design project structure (data layer, query engine, MCP server, tests)","status":"completed","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement CSV loading and team-name/date normalization","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement query logic for matches, teams, players, competitions, and stats","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Implement MCP server over stdio with required tools","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write BDD-style pytest test suite","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Run tests and fix failures","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Verify build/install and update README","status":"pending","priority":"medium"}],"truncated":false},"title":"6 todos","time":{"start":1782358219459,"end":1782358219462}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"             The 2020 champion is 'atletico' with 171 pts etc., but that seems inflated due to duplicates across datasets. Wait we used only Brasileirao_Matches and still got 18 teams and 94 matches per team? Actually Brasileirao_Matches has 110 matches per round? number of matches per season ~380, points total per match ~2, so season total points ~760. If champion has 171, that's plausible? Actually 20 teams x 38 matches = 760 matches. Champion with 171 means avg ~1.33 per team? Wait champion wins ~55%? 171 = 47*3+30 = 171, matches 114? That's not possible in one season; Brasileirão has 38 matches. So duplicates within the file? Maybe `Brasileirao_Matches.csv` has duplicate rows? Let me check unique matches count per season.\n\nHome record earlier for Corinthians 2022 gave 19 matches (makes sense, 19 home). But if total matches per team per season is 38, why champion Atletico has 114 matches? Because we didn't filter out NULL scores? Wait our canon 'atletico' matches both Atlético-MG and Atlético Paranaense? We stripped accent and state's? In our temp test we used canon that collapses Atlético-MG and Athletico/Atlético-PR to 'atletico'? Yes we removed 'Atlético' accent and not preserving state, so Atlético-MG, Atlético-PR, Athletico-PR all map to 'atletico'. That artificially merged teams. Our real canonicalization preserves state suffix, so Atlético-MG -> 'atleticomg'. Good. So the inflated points are due to temporary collapse. In real code, 'atleticomg' champions. Need compute 2020 standings with proper canonical. But not needed for tests; we can assert champion contains 'Atlético' and points near 80-ish.\n\nAlso 2020 bottom 4 includes Vasco da Gama, Goiás, Coritiba, Botafogo. Good.\n\nNow check 2019 with state suffix preservation. Flamengo champion. Good.\n\nNeed ensure Copa do Brasil finals: in Brazilian_Cup_Matches round 8 (max). But if query \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\" we can implement special handling: determine max round per season and filter. But simpler: tool `find_matches(competition='Copa do Brasil', round='8')`. However the natural language query would be handled by LLM using tools; but LLM might call with round 'final'. We can allow `round` to accept 'final' and convert to max round per season? Could implement in find_matches: if round parameter is 'final', compute max round for competition/season and filter. But just include a tool `competition_finals(competition, season=None)`? Maybe not necessary; just tests can call round=8.\n\nSpec wants ability to answer \"Find all Copa do Brasil finals\". We can provide tool with round param. In test we use round='8' and verify matches decreased. But to better support natural language, maybe add a tool `get_finals(competition, season=None)` that returns matches whose round is the maximum round for that season/competition. I'll add `find_finals(competition, season=None)` returning matches with the highest round in the dataset. That maps to finals. But maybe not needed. Let's add `competition_finals` tool.\n\nSimilarly \"Show the 2018 Copa Libertadores bracket\": filter competition Copa Libertadores season 2018, return matches grouped by stage. Could use `find_matches(competition='Copa Libertadores', season=2018)` and present sorted by stage. That's okay.\n\nNow design server return text. Use a helper to format match lines. The tools should return human-readable.\n\nAlso we need to consider that `FastMCP` may call tool functions concurrently; our engine state is read-only after initialization, safe.\n\nPotential issue: Loading mcp from outside venv? It's installed in `/Users/maui/dve/experiments/retort/.venv`. Python we're using may be from that venv (site-packages). Need check `sys.prefix`. Actually `python3` command uses the user environment with venv active? The mcp path shows venv. So it's accessible. Good.\n\nNow begin implementation. I will marker todo inspect done and design in progress maybe.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efcd40e28001KWH1rZ5qvNyjfz","sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","messageID":"msg_efcd3dfe6001nGtjtuWGxIih1O"}}
