l Serie A records. That's why Corinthians 2022 with `competition='Brasileirão'` returned no matches: because its records maybe from BR-Football labeled \"Série A\". We must map \"Serie A\" to \"Brasileirão\" as per spec. \"Série B\"/C should maybe map to \"Brasileirão Série B\"? But for consistency with spec, map Serie A to Brasileirão. Serie B and Serie C are not requested but could still be queried by exact name. But if we map Serie B to \"Brasileirão\" then queries for \"Brasileirão\" would include B/C matches, which may be undesirable. However the spec says competition queries for Brasileirão. The data includes Serie A, B, C. We should map Serie A to \"Brasileirão\"; keep Serie B/C as distinct or map \"Serie B\" to \"Brasileirão Série B\"? For simple, treat only Serie A as Brasileirão. Currently code maps Serie A to \"Série A\" not \"Brasileirão\". Fix.\n\n2. 2019 standings champion says \"Atletico - 119 pts\" due to potentially merging Athletico/Atletico variants? Wait our canonicalization preserves state suffix and aliases 'athletico' -> 'atletico', so Atlético-MG = 'atleticomg', Athletico-PR = 'atleticopr'. They shouldn't merge. Why 119 pts? Maybe because 2019 matches are duplicated between novo_campeonato_brasileiro and Brasileirao_Matches (2019 both). After dedup, should not duplicate. But perhaps date formats differ causing not deduped? `Brasileirao_Matches` dates are 'YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS'; `novo` dates 'DD/MM/YYYY'. parse_date handles both, should produce same date. However dedupe key includes competition, season, home_canonical, away_canonical, date. Season: both 2019, home/away canonical: should match? Let's verify one match. But champion \"Atletico\" not \"Flamengo\"? Actually we expected Flamengo 90 pts. Our standings computed from all matches, maybe includes Fre Flamengo from multiple sources? Could be dedup didn't merge due to team name canonical differences: e.g., \"Flamengo\" vs \"Flamengo-RJ\". We strip state suffix, so both canonical 'flamengo'. Should merge. Maybe the \"Atletico\" key is actually Atlético-MG (atleticomg) and it has 119 pts because Atlético-MG matches appear in both sources and dedup failed due to different dates? Or because `Brasileirao_Matches` has each match duplicated multiple times for betting lines? Wait dataset maybe has rows for multiple bookmakers? No.\n\nWait we saw `Atletico` as champion in 2019 from novo alone earlier with 90? Actually earlier we computed 2019 novo champion Flamengo with 90. Why combined gives Atletico 119? Hmm.\n\nLet's inspect 2019 Brasileirão team counts and points. We can compute from deduped matches and see raw counts per team.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efcd97ee4001SgZ6B4AQBsxH0t","sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","messageID":"msg_efcd9462400163FdrhX54QDyni"}}
