{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782358671675,"sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"functions.edit:39","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a two-letter state code at the end of\n# a team name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" or \"Palmeiras - SP\".\n_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n\n# Matches a parenthetical state/country code at the end, e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\".\n_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*\\)$\")\n\n# Removes parenthetical explanations such as\n# \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\".\n_PARENS_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\")","oldString":"# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a two-letter state code at the end of\n# a team name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" or \"Palmeiro - SP\".\n_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n\n# Removes parenthetical explanations such as\n# \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\".\n_PARENS_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\")"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -17,8 +17,11 @@\n # Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a two-letter state code at the end of\n # a team name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" or \"Palmeiras - SP\".\n _STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n \n+# Matches a parenthetical state/country code at the end, e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\".\n+_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*\\)$\")\n+\n # Removes parenthetical explanations such as\n # \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\".\n _PARENS_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\")\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -17,8 +17,11 @@\n # Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a two-letter state code at the end of\n # a team name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" or \"Palmeiras - SP\".\n _STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n \n+# Matches a parenthetical state/country code at the end, e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\".\n+_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*\\)$\")\n+\n # Removes parenthetical explanations such as\n # \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\".\n _PARENS_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\")\n \n","additions":3,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1782358671670,"end":1782358671672}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"                               Also 'Atletico Goianiense'/GO etc. Need map these too. Good. So ambiguous root 'atletico' and descriptors GO, MG, PR, plus others. We can map suffix state code for all; for \"Atletico Goianiense\" descriptor 'goianiense' -> GO. So descriptor map should include goianiense -> go. For 'FC Atlético Cearense' descriptor 'cearense' -> ce. Need comprehensive enough.\n\nBut simpler: Use descriptor map and state suffix to canonical. For ambiguous root, base may already include descriptor; we can infer state from descriptor. Let's implement robust `canonical_team_name` that:\n1. Extract explicit state suffix ` - XX` or `-XX` at end => explicit_state.\n2. Remove parentheses.\n3. Strip accents and punctuation -> raw_key lower + digits.\n4. Apply `athletico` -> `atletico` alias.\n5. Determine root and descriptor:\n   - If raw_key starts with one of AMBIGUOUS roots, root = that. The rest = tail.\n   - Else root = raw_key (no state, no descriptor). Return root (maybe append state? For non-ambiguous, I think strip state to merge; so return root).\n6. For ambiguous root, infer state:\n   - Use explicit_state if present.\n   - Else search tail for DESCRIPTOR_STATE mapping.\n   - Else state = ''.\n7. Return canonical = root + state (lowercase).\n\nNeed also handle \"America\"? Remove accent -> america. Ambiguous root. \"América-MG\" -> root america state mg -> americamg. \"America-RN\" etc. \"América de Natal\" descriptor? Actually \"América FC (Minas Gerais)\" maybe descriptor 'minasgerais' -> mg? Could add minas -> mg.\n\nWhat about Sport? \"Sport Club do Recife\" root sport, tail \"clubdorecife\" state? No explicit suffix. Descriptor? 'recifense' not present. But `Brasileirao_Matches` likely has \"Sport-PE\" -> explicit_state PE -> sportpe. \"Sport Club do Recife\" in other dataset would not match because no state and no recife descriptor. We can add descriptor for recife -> pe maybe? Tail contains 'recife'. Map 'recife' -> pe. Then \"Sport Club do Recife\" canonical 'sportpe'. Good. But \"sport\" query should match both. The `_keys_match` substring handles query 'sport' in 'sportpe'? query base 'sport', team key 'sportpe', substring yes. Good. But ambiguous between Sport Recife and other Sport? There may be \"Sport - MG\"? Not common. Fine.\n\nNacional: \"Nacional-URU\" explicit state 'URU' (not a Brazilian state) -> nacionaluru. \"Nacional\" alone root nacional state '' -> nacional. Query 'Nacional' matches both. Fine.\n\nBotafogo: \"Botafogo-RJ\" botafogorj, \"Botafogo-PB\" botafogopb. There are \"Botafogo FR\"? root botafogo, tail 'fr' no state; maybe 'botafogosp'? We may not identify, but rare.\n\nVitoria: \"Vitória-BA\" root vitoria state ba -> vitoriaba. Query 'Vitória' matches.\n\nAnother issue: \"América (MG)\" parentheses? We strip parenthetical; state suffix extracted before parentheses? Wait name \"América (MG)\" has parentheses, not suffix. Our state suffix regex searches for `-XX` at end; parentheses will prevent match. Then we strip parentheses -> \"América\", losing MG. Could improve state extraction to also capture parentheses with two letters: `(...)` ending. But BR-Football might have \"América MG\"? Let's see. Not critical now. We can add `(...)` state extraction: if after removing parentheses, the remaining ends with state suffix. For parenthetical state inside, we can detect pattern `\\(([A-Z]{2})\\)$` after suffix extraction fails. Let's handle both. Also \"Nacional (URU)\" has suffix inside parentheses; explicit_state URU. Root nacional, tail '', state = explicit URU -> nacionaluru.\n\nBut for \"América (MG)\" root america, state explicit MG -> americamg.\n\nImplement this in normalize. Then recompute and re-test.\n\nAlso fix competition_canonical to map Serie A -> Brasileirão. For Serie B/C maybe keep separate.\n\nLet's edit normalize.py.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efcdae1ac001otvC4MArgYLvW9","sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","messageID":"msg_efcda939a001BAr6wPIRIWr8Sk"}}
