{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782358744413,"sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"functions.edit:43","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"# Collapses punctuation and whitespace for canonical keys.\n_NON_ALNUM_RE = re.compile(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\")\n\n# Roots that are shared by several distinct clubs. For these we keep a state\n# code so that, for example, Atlético-MG and Atlético-PR remain separate.\nAMBIGUOUS_ROOTS = (\n    \"atletico\",\n    \"sport\",\n    \"america\",\n    \"nacional\",\n    \"botafogo\",\n    \"vitoria\",\n    \"victoria\",\n    \"portuguesa\",\n    \"santa\",\n)\n\n# Map trailing descriptors to state/country codes. Used when a dataset gives\n# the long form of an ambiguous team name without a numeric state suffix.\nDESCRIPTOR_STATE = {\n    \"mineiro\": \"mg\",\n    \"mineira\": \"mg\",\n    \"paranaense\": \"pr\",\n    \"parana\": \"pr\",\n    \"goianiense\": \"go\",\n    \"goiano\": \"go\",\n    \"cearense\": \"ce\",\n    \"ceara\": \"ce\",\n    \"baiano\": \"ba\",\n    \"bahia\": \"ba\",\n    \"paulista\": \"sp\",\n    \"paulistano\": \"sp\",\n    \"carioca\": \"rj\",\n    \"gaucho\": \"rs\",\n    \"gaucha\": \"rs\",\n    \"potiguar\": \"rn\",\n    \"pernambucano\": \"pe\",\n    \"pernambucana\": \"pe\",\n    \"recifense\": \"pe\",\n    \"recife\": \"pe\",\n    \"fluminense\": \"rj\",\n    \"amazonense\": \"am\",\n    \"paraense\": \"pa\",\n    \"sergipano\": \"se\",\n    \"sergipana\": \"se\",\n    \"catarinense\": \"sc\",\n    \"matogrossense\": \"mt\",\n    \"matogrosso\": \"mt\",\n    \"sulmatogrossense\": \"ms\",\n    \"sulmatogrosso\": \"ms\",\n    \"rondoniense\": \"ro\",\n    \"capixaba\": \"es\",\n    \"maranhense\": \"ma\",\n    \"paraibano\": \"pb\",\n    \"piauiense\": \"pi\",\n    \"alagoano\": \"al\",\n    \"alagoana\": \"al\",\n    \"brasiliense\": \"df\",\n    \"brasilia\": \"df\",\n}\n\n# A small set of aliases that map historical/typographic variants to a shared\n# canonical base **before** appending the state suffix. This keeps\n# Atlético-MG distinct from Athletico-PR while still recognising the\n# Athletico -> Atlético rebranding.\n_BASE_ALIASES: list[tuple[re.Pattern, str]] = [\n    (re.compile(r\"^athletico\"), \"atletico\"),  # Athletico Paranaense\n]\n\n# Friendly display aliases for common shorthand used in queries.\nDISPLAY_ALIASES = {","oldString":"# Collapses punctuation and whitespace for canonical keys.\n_NON_ALNUM_RE = re.compile(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\")\n\n# A small set of aliases that map historical/typographic variants to a shared\n# canonical base **before** appending the state suffix. This keeps\n# Atlético-MG distinct from Athletico-PR while still recognising the\n# Athletico -> Atlético rebranding.\n_BASE_ALIASES: list[tuple[re.Pattern, str]] = [\n    (re.compile(r\"^athletico\"), \"atletico\"),  # Athletico Paranaense\n]\n\n# Friendly display aliases for common shorthand used in queries.\nDISPLAY_ALIASES = {"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -27,8 +27,66 @@\n \n # Collapses punctuation and whitespace for canonical keys.\n _NON_ALNUM_RE = re.compile(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\")\n \n+# Roots that are shared by several distinct clubs. For these we keep a state\n+# code so that, for example, Atlético-MG and Atlético-PR remain separate.\n+AMBIGUOUS_ROOTS = (\n+    \"atletico\",\n+    \"sport\",\n+    \"america\",\n+    \"nacional\",\n+    \"botafogo\",\n+    \"vitoria\",\n+    \"victoria\",\n+    \"portuguesa\",\n+    \"santa\",\n+)\n+\n+# Map trailing descriptors to state/country codes. Used when a dataset gives\n+# the long form of an ambiguous team name without a numeric state suffix.\n+DESCRIPTOR_STATE = {\n+    \"mineiro\": \"mg\",\n+    \"mineira\": \"mg\",\n+    \"paranaense\": \"pr\",\n+    \"parana\": \"pr\",\n+    \"goianiense\": \"go\",\n+    \"goiano\": \"go\",\n+    \"cearense\": \"ce\",\n+    \"ceara\": \"ce\",\n+    \"baiano\": \"ba\",\n+    \"bahia\": \"ba\",\n+    \"paulista\": \"sp\",\n+    \"paulistano\": \"sp\",\n+    \"carioca\": \"rj\",\n+    \"gaucho\": \"rs\",\n+    \"gaucha\": \"rs\",\n+    \"potiguar\": \"rn\",\n+    \"pernambucano\": \"pe\",\n+    \"pernambucana\": \"pe\",\n+    \"recifense\": \"pe\",\n+    \"recife\": \"pe\",\n+    \"fluminense\": \"rj\",\n+    \"amazonense\": \"am\",\n+    \"paraense\": \"pa\",\n+    \"sergipano\": \"se\",\n+    \"sergipana\": \"se\",\n+    \"catarinense\": \"sc\",\n+    \"matogrossense\": \"mt\",\n+    \"matogrosso\": \"mt\",\n+    \"sulmatogrossense\": \"ms\",\n+    \"sulmatogrosso\": \"ms\",\n+    \"rondoniense\": \"ro\",\n+    \"capixaba\": \"es\",\n+    \"maranhense\": \"ma\",\n+    \"paraibano\": \"pb\",\n+    \"piauiense\": \"pi\",\n+    \"alagoano\": \"al\",\n+    \"alagoana\": \"al\",\n+    \"brasiliense\": \"df\",\n+    \"brasilia\": \"df\",\n+}\n+\n # A small set of aliases that map historical/typographic variants to a shared\n # canonical base **before** appending the state suffix. This keeps\n # Atlético-MG distinct from Athletico-PR while still recognising the\n # Athletico -> Atlético rebranding.\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -27,8 +27,66 @@\n \n # Collapses punctuation and whitespace for canonical keys.\n _NON_ALNUM_RE = re.compile(r\"[^a-z0-9]+\")\n \n+# Roots that are shared by several distinct clubs. For these we keep a state\n+# code so that, for example, Atlético-MG and Atlético-PR remain separate.\n+AMBIGUOUS_ROOTS = (\n+    \"atletico\",\n+    \"sport\",\n+    \"america\",\n+    \"nacional\",\n+    \"botafogo\",\n+    \"vitoria\",\n+    \"victoria\",\n+    \"portuguesa\",\n+    \"santa\",\n+)\n+\n+# Map trailing descriptors to state/country codes. Used when a dataset gives\n+# the long form of an ambiguous team name without a numeric state suffix.\n+DESCRIPTOR_STATE = {\n+    \"mineiro\": \"mg\",\n+    \"mineira\": \"mg\",\n+    \"paranaense\": \"pr\",\n+    \"parana\": \"pr\",\n+    \"goianiense\": \"go\",\n+    \"goiano\": \"go\",\n+    \"cearense\": \"ce\",\n+    \"ceara\": \"ce\",\n+    \"baiano\": \"ba\",\n+    \"bahia\": \"ba\",\n+    \"paulista\": \"sp\",\n+    \"paulistano\": \"sp\",\n+    \"carioca\": \"rj\",\n+    \"gaucho\": \"rs\",\n+    \"gaucha\": \"rs\",\n+    \"potiguar\": \"rn\",\n+    \"pernambucano\": \"pe\",\n+    \"pernambucana\": \"pe\",\n+    \"recifense\": \"pe\",\n+    \"recife\": \"pe\",\n+    \"fluminense\": \"rj\",\n+    \"amazonense\": \"am\",\n+    \"paraense\": \"pa\",\n+    \"sergipano\": \"se\",\n+    \"sergipana\": \"se\",\n+    \"catarinense\": \"sc\",\n+    \"matogrossense\": \"mt\",\n+    \"matogrosso\": \"mt\",\n+    \"sulmatogrossense\": \"ms\",\n+    \"sulmatogrosso\": \"ms\",\n+    \"rondoniense\": \"ro\",\n+    \"capixaba\": \"es\",\n+    \"maranhense\": \"ma\",\n+    \"paraibano\": \"pb\",\n+    \"piauiense\": \"pi\",\n+    \"alagoano\": \"al\",\n+    \"alagoana\": \"al\",\n+    \"brasiliense\": \"df\",\n+    \"brasilia\": \"df\",\n+}\n+\n # A small set of aliases that map historical/typographic variants to a shared\n # canonical base **before** appending the state suffix. This keeps\n # Atlético-MG distinct from Athletico-PR while still recognising the\n # Athletico -> Atlético rebranding.\n","additions":58,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1782358744409,"end":1782358744412}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"                               novo also uses Botafogo-RJ (so suffix present). BR-Football has \"Botafogo RJ\" (space). Our state suffix regex allows whitespace before and after dash? It expects `-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$` so \"Botafogo RJ\" doesn't match because missing dash. Need handle space-separated state codes like \"Botafogo RJ\". The existing regex accounts for `-` before state but not zero dash with space. We can change to match optional dash and spaces: `r\"(?:-\\s*)?([A-Z]{2})$\"`? But that would match \"Botafogo RJ\" where space before RJ. However it could also match final word as state if name ends with 2-letter word (e.g., \"ABC FC\" no). Could be ambiguous. But for teams like \"Botafogo RJ\" we want to extract RJ. Also \"America MG\"? Let's see. So regex should be flexible: `\\s+-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$` or `\\s+([A-Z]{2})$`? Use pattern: `r\"(?:\\s*-\\s*|\\s+)([A-Z]{2})$\"`. But this would match \"São Paulo SP\" and strip SP, fine. For \"Nacional (URU)\", parens regex.\n\nAlso \"EC Bahia\"? no suffix. \"Fortaleza FC\" has FC not state. \"Ceará SC\"? state code SC at end? \"Ceará\" no. \"Vitória-BA\". Good.\n\nMaybe also BR-Football has \"Athletico Paranaense\" (no suffix) and \"Botafogo SP\". We map 'paranaense' descriptor for atletico, and 'Botafogo SP' via space state extraction to botafogosp. Good.\n\nChange `_STATE_SUFFIX_RE` to capture optional dash/space state.\n\nAlso for \"Fortaleza FC\" ends with 'FC' uppercase, not state. Good.\n\nFor \"Cruzeiro EC\" not issue.\n\nNow update `_clean_base` and `canonical_team_name` with descriptor/ambiguous logic.\n\nLet's write new normalize section. We'll replace `_clean_base` and `canonical_team_name` and competition_canonical. Use edit blocks.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efcdbe0c3001dDTEwkswYTahJU","sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","messageID":"msg_efcdbae7e001RXhS7E0iqKtY2t"}}
