{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1782358799813,"sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"functions.edit:45","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","newString":"# Brazilian state/country codes that sometimes appear as trailing suffixes.\n_STATE_CODES = (\n    \"AC\", \"AL\", \"AP\", \"AM\", \"BA\", \"CE\", \"DF\", \"ES\", \"GO\", \"MA\", \"MT\", \"MS\", \"MG\",\n    \"PA\", \"PB\", \"PR\", \"PE\", \"PI\", \"RJ\", \"RN\", \"RS\", \"RO\", \"RR\", \"SC\", \"SP\", \"SE\", \"TO\",\n    # Common international codes seen in the Libertadores dataset.\n    \"URU\", \"ARG\", \"BRA\", \"CHI\", \"COL\", \"ECU\", \"PAR\", \"PER\", \"VEN\", \"BOL\",\n)\n\n# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a state code at the end of a team\n# name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Palmeiras - SP\" or \"Botafogo RJ\".\n_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"(?:\\s*-\\s*|\\s+)(\" + \"|\".join(_STATE_CODES) + r\")$\")\n\n# Matches a parenthetical state/country code at the end, e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\".\n_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*(\" + \"|\".join(_STATE_CODES) + r\")\\s*\\)$\")","oldString":"# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a two-letter state code at the end of\n# a team name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" or \"Palmeiras - SP\".\n_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n\n# Matches a parenthetical state/country code at the end, e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\".\n_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*\\)$\")"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -13,14 +13,22 @@\n import unicodedata\n from datetime import date, datetime\n from typing import Optional\n \n-# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a two-letter state code at the end of\n-# a team name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" or \"Palmeiras - SP\".\n-_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n+# Brazilian state/country codes that sometimes appear as trailing suffixes.\n+_STATE_CODES = (\n+    \"AC\", \"AL\", \"AP\", \"AM\", \"BA\", \"CE\", \"DF\", \"ES\", \"GO\", \"MA\", \"MT\", \"MS\", \"MG\",\n+    \"PA\", \"PB\", \"PR\", \"PE\", \"PI\", \"RJ\", \"RN\", \"RS\", \"RO\", \"RR\", \"SC\", \"SP\", \"SE\", \"TO\",\n+    # Common international codes seen in the Libertadores dataset.\n+    \"URU\", \"ARG\", \"BRA\", \"CHI\", \"COL\", \"ECU\", \"PAR\", \"PER\", \"VEN\", \"BOL\",\n+)\n \n+# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a state code at the end of a team\n+# name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Palmeiras - SP\" or \"Botafogo RJ\".\n+_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"(?:\\s*-\\s*|\\s+)(\" + \"|\".join(_STATE_CODES) + r\")$\")\n+\n # Matches a parenthetical state/country code at the end, e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\".\n-_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*\\)$\")\n+_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*(\" + \"|\".join(_STATE_CODES) + r\")\\s*\\)$\")\n \n # Removes parenthetical explanations such as\n # \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\".\n _PARENS_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\")\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -13,14 +13,22 @@\n import unicodedata\n from datetime import date, datetime\n from typing import Optional\n \n-# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a two-letter state code at the end of\n-# a team name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\" or \"Palmeiras - SP\".\n-_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\")\n+# Brazilian state/country codes that sometimes appear as trailing suffixes.\n+_STATE_CODES = (\n+    \"AC\", \"AL\", \"AP\", \"AM\", \"BA\", \"CE\", \"DF\", \"ES\", \"GO\", \"MA\", \"MT\", \"MS\", \"MG\",\n+    \"PA\", \"PB\", \"PR\", \"PE\", \"PI\", \"RJ\", \"RN\", \"RS\", \"RO\", \"RR\", \"SC\", \"SP\", \"SE\", \"TO\",\n+    # Common international codes seen in the Libertadores dataset.\n+    \"URU\", \"ARG\", \"BRA\", \"CHI\", \"COL\", \"ECU\", \"PAR\", \"PER\", \"VEN\", \"BOL\",\n+)\n \n+# Matches optional whitespace, a dash and a state code at the end of a team\n+# name, e.g. \"Palmeiras-SP\", \"Palmeiras - SP\" or \"Botafogo RJ\".\n+_STATE_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"(?:\\s*-\\s*|\\s+)(\" + \"|\".join(_STATE_CODES) + r\")$\")\n+\n # Matches a parenthetical state/country code at the end, e.g. \"Nacional (URU)\".\n-_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*([A-Z]{2})\\s*\\)$\")\n+_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\(\\s*(\" + \"|\".join(_STATE_CODES) + r\")\\s*\\)$\")\n \n # Removes parenthetical explanations such as\n # \"Boavista Sport Club (antigo Esporte Clube Barreira)\".\n _PARENS_RE = re.compile(r\"\\s*\\([^)]*\\)\")\n","additions":12,"deletions":4},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1782358799809,"end":1782358799812}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"                                        Need also update `_STATE_SUFFIX_RE` to capture space-separated state codes. Currently `r\"\\s*-\\s*([A-Z]{2})$\"`. Let's change to `(?:\\s*-\\s*|\\s+)([A-Z]{2,3})$` to allow 2-3 letters. But using \\s+ would treat last word as state for any 2-3 uppercase final token. For \"FC Porto\" -> 'FC' not state (still, 'FC' is uppercase length 2). Could cause false extraction. But Brazilian clubs generally not ending with such. However e.g., \"SC Corinthians\"? 'SC' could be stripped. That would be bad. Need be careful. Better regex: require dash before state OR parentheses. But \"Botafogo RJ\" lacks dash. Data uses \"Botafogo RJ\" and \"Botafogo PB\" as two words. Maybe other BR-Football teams: \"Fortaleza FC\"? It would match FC falsely if \\s+ allowed. So we can't allow space-only without dash for generic names. Instead, we can detect known state abbreviations after space with a positive lookahead? Better keep state suffix regex dash-based, and separately handle BR-Football style names: if a name ends with a known 2-letter Brazilian state code preceded by space, treat it as state. But we need list of known state codes to avoid stripping \"FC\". Let's add a list of brazilian state codes and country codes. Or simply handle known state codes at end.\n\nWe can create `KNOWN_STATES = { 'AC','AL','AP','AM','BA','CE','DF','ES','GO','MA','MT','MS','MG','PA','PB','PR','PE','PI','RJ','RN','RS','RO','RR','SC','SP','SE','TO','URU','ARG','CHI','COL','ECU','PAR','PER','VEN','BOL','URU' ... }`. Then after removing parens suffix (e.g., Nacional (URU)), if no explicit state, split last word and if it is in KNOWN_STATES and separated by space, treat as state. This will strip RJ from \"Botafogo RJ\", but also \"Cruzeiro EC\" -> last 'EC' not known; 'SC' is state Santa Catarina, but also abbreviation for Sport Club. That could affect \"Sport Club\" ending with SC? Not common at end. \"Clube Náutico Capibaribe\" no. \"Avaí SC\"? In BR-Football maybe \"Avaí SC\"? We can tolerate. But \" Sport Club do Recife\" no. \"Figueirense SC\"? Could be. Fine.\n\nBut we can avoid stripping generic abbreviations by only stripping if the token before is not a common org suffix: FC, EC, SC (as suffix). Hard. Let's list known state codes; 'SC' is state but also suffix. Some teams \"Sport Club\" not end with SC. Many clubs end in \"EC\" or \"FC\". Not states. Good.\n\nImplement _STATE_SUFFIX_RE with specific states plus dash or space? Simpler: in `_clean_base`, after dash extraction, check last token. Use regex that captures optional dash/space but verifies the captured code in known states. For more safety, the regex can be: `r\"(?:\\s*-\\s*|\\s+)(AC|AL|AP|AM|BA|CE|DF|ES|GO|MA|MT|MS|MG|PA|PB|PR|PE|PI|RJ|RN|RS|RO|RR|SC|SP|SE|TO|URU|ARG|BRA|CHI|COL|ECU|PAR|PER|VEN|BOL)$\"` with prefix space or dash. This will match \"Botafogo RJ\" and \"Botafogo-RJ\" and not \"Cruzeiro EC\" if EC not in list. Good.\n\nLet's define `_STATE_CODES` tuple and build regex. Replace `_STATE_SUFFIX_RE` and `_PARENS_SUFFIX_RE` patterns accordingly. We need 2-3 letter codes.\n\nLet's edit regex and ensure `KNOWN_STATE_CODES` accessible? Not needed elsewhere.\n\nUse edit to modify variable definitions.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efcdccaa7001yAUBWk1DHIX39i","sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","messageID":"msg_efcdc8ec70016zEAhGND7dsSCQ"}}
