"NFKD\", text) if unicodedata.category(c) != \"Mn\"\n","filediff":{"file":"/private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","patch":"Index: /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n===================================================================\n--- /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n+++ /private/var/folders/t6/p1v727892_qc9xqqdzq2rpym0000gn/T/retort-local-tjpsd7_l/retort-8ea0ffcc10d3/brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py\n@@ -109,9 +109,63 @@\n     \"mengao\": \"Flamengo\",\n     \"galo\": \"Atlético Mineiro\",\n }\n \n+# Map specific raw canonical forms produced by different datasets to a shared\n+# canonical key. This removes duplicates that arise from different naming\n+# styles such as \"Red Bull Bragantino\" vs \"Bragantino\" or \"EC Juventude\"\n+# vs \"Juventude\".\n+TEAM_CANONICAL_ALIASES: dict[str, str] = {\n+    \"redbullbragantino\": \"bragantino\",\n+    \"bragantinosp\": \"bragantino\",\n+    \"ecjuventude\": \"juventude\",\n+    \"juventude\": \"juventude\",\n+    \"esporteclubejuventude\": \"juventude\",\n+    \"fortalezafc\": \"fortaleza\",\n+    \"fortalezace\": \"fortaleza\",\n+    \"clubederegatasdoflamengo\": \"flamengo\",\n+    \"flamengorj\": \"flamengo\",\n+    \"sportclubcorinthianspaulista\": \"corinthians\",\n+    \"corinthianssp\": \"corinthians\",\n+    \"saopaulofutebolclube\": \"saopaulo\",\n+    \"saopaulofc\": \"saopaulo\",\n+    \"santosfutebolclube\": \"santos\",\n+    \"santosfc\": \"santos\",\n+    \"gremiofootballportoalegrense\": \"gremio\",\n+    \"gremiors\": \"gremio\",\n+    \"sportclubinternacional\": \"internacional\",\n+    \"internacionalrs\": \"internacional\",\n+    \"cluberecrionegra\": \"vasco\",\n+    \"vascodagama\": \"vasco\",\n+    \"vascorj\": \"vasco\",\n+    \"fluminensefootballclub\": \"fluminense\",\n+    \"fluminenserj\": \"fluminense\",\n+    \"esporteclubebahia\": \"bahia\",\n+    \"bahiaba\": \"bahia\",\n+    \"cearasc\": \"ceara\",\n+    \"paranaclube\": \"parana\",\n+    \"avaisc\": \"avai\",\n+    \"goiasesporteclube\": \"goias\",\n+    \"americamineiro\": \"americamg\",\n+    \"americafcmg\": \"americamg\",\n+    \"botafogodefuteboleregentas\": \"botafogorj\",\n+    \"botafogorj\": \"botafogorj\",\n+    \"botafogofr\": \"botafogorj\",\n+    \"botafogofutebolclube\": \"botafogorj\",\n+    \"pontepreta\": \"pontepreta\",\n+    \"associacaoatleticapontepreta\": \"pontepreta\",\n+    \"criciumaesporteclube\": \"criciuma\",\n+    \"figueirensefc\": \"figueirense\",\n+    \"chapecoenseaf\": \"chapecoense\",\n+    \"nautico\": \"nautico\",\n+    \"clubenautico\": \"nautico\",\n+    \"londrinaesporteclube\": \"londrina\",\n+    \"csa\": \"csaal\",\n+    \"csaal\": \"csaal\",\n+    \"csaalagoas\": \"csaal\",\n+}\n \n+\n def strip_accents(text: str) -> str:\n     \"\"\"Return an ASCII-fied version of *text* with diacritics removed.\"\"\"\n     return \"\".join(\n         c for c in unicodedata.normalize(\"NFKD\", text) if unicodedata.category(c) != \"Mn\"\n","additions":54,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"brazilian_soccer_mcp/normalize.py","time":{"start":1782359092924,"end":1782359092927}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"                                                        Good. 'clubederegatasdoflamengo' is a distinct key for full name. That appears from full-name variants? It will not be matched by 'Flamengo' substring? 'flamengo' substring in 'clubederegatasdoflamengo' yes (because in team key). So stats query returns it. But for standings, it's separate. Need alias full names to base. Query matching substring already unifies. For standings, we can canonicalise all teams using the same matching logic rather than exact canonical? `_compute_standings` uses raw canonical. Could map full names by maintaining a mapping from team display/clean to canonical base and applying before standings. But perhaps easier: after loading data, normalise all canonical keys by consulting display name lookup? We could create a \"preferred canonical\" mapping: for each display name (after stripping state/parentheses), compute base canonical, and map every longer canonical containing it to it? But this could over-collapse.\n\nGiven complexity, I think it's acceptable to have some duplicate team entries for long/full names. Tests can focus on queries that use substring matching, not exact standings totals. For \"Who won 2019 Brasileirão?\" answer lists Flamengo champion but with inflated points; we can assert Flamengo appears in champion line and not crash. That's fine.\n\nBut for sample tests like Corinthians 2022 home record, the spec example expects 19 matches. Our result 22 due to duplicate fixtures (opponent variants) not due to team name canonical of Corinthians. Could we improve merging of opponent variants to reduce to 38? The duplicate opponents list shows variants for 'bragantino'/'redbullbragantino', 'ecjuventude'/'juventude', 'fortaleza'/'fortalezafc'. We can add explicit alias map to merge these. Let's add a `TEAM_ALIASES` dict mapping canonical of known variants to target canonical. Apply in `_make_match` after computing canonical. That will unify in data.\n\nAlso for \"Flamengo\" full name, add alias 'clubederegatasdoflamengo' -> 'flamengo'. But where does full name occur? In `Brazilian_Cup_Matches` maybe long names include full. Could add.\n\nSimilarly 'sportclubcorinthianspaulista' -> 'corinthians', 'saopaulofc' -> 'saopaulo', 'santosfc' -> 'santos', 'gremiofbpa' -> 'gremio'. But these may not affect.\n\nLet's implement an alias mapping in data_loader. We'll add `TEAM_ALIASES` and apply both `home_canonical` and `away_canonical` in `_make_match`.\n\nBut be careful not to collapse ambiguous variants incorrectly. Keep alias local to known duplicates.\n\nMap:\n- 'redbullbragantino' -> 'bragantino'\n- 'ecjuventude' -> 'juventude'\n- 'fortalezafc' -> 'fortaleza'\n- 'clubederegatasdoflamengo' -> 'flamengo'\n- 'sportclubcorinthianspaulista' -> 'corinthians'\n- 'santosfutebolclube' -> 'santos'\n- 'saopaulofutebolclube' -> 'saopaulo'\n- 'clubeatleticomineiro' -> 'atleticomg'\n- 'clubeatleticoparanaense'/'atleticoparanaense' -> 'atleticopr'\n- 'gremiofootballportoalegrense' -> 'gremio'\n- 'sportclubinternacional' -> 'internacional'\n- 'esporteclubebahia' -> 'bahia'\n- 'fluminensefootballclub' -> 'fluminense'\n- 'clubederegatasvasco'/'vasco' -> 'vascodagama'? Actually Vasco query matches. But 'vascodagama' vs 'vasco' keys. Query returns both. We can map 'vascodagama' -> 'vasco'? But display. Maybe not necessary.\n- 'americamineiro'/'americamg' -> 'americamg'? same.\n- 'ceara' vs 'cearasc' maybe.\n\nAlso 'ponte preta' full names. But enough for demos.\n\nBut actually, the canonical for 'Atlético-MG' from `Brasileirao_Matches` is 'atleticomg', and from `BR-Football` 'Atletico Mineiro' descriptor -> 'atleticomg'. Good. 'Club Atlético Mineiro' full name raw_key 'clubeatleticomineiro', root 'atletico' with tail 'clubeatleticomineiro' descriptor mineiro => 'atleticomg'. Already good. 'Clube Atlético Paranaense': root atletico, descriptor paranaense -> atleticopr. Good.\n\n'Red Bull Bragantino' raw_key 'redbullbragantino' not ambiguous, returns that. Need alias. 'Bragantino' returns 'bragantino'. Fine.\n\n'EC Juventude' returns 'ecjuventude'; alias to 'juventude'. 'Esporte Clube Juventude' raw_key 'esporteclubejuventude', root? 'esporteclube' not ambiguous, so returns long. Hmm maybe a better approach to strip common prefixes. But 'EC Juventude' is BR-Football; 'Esporte Clube Juventude' maybe not. We'll alias 'ecjuventude'.\n\n'Fortaleza FC' -> 'fortalezafc'; alias to 'fortaleza'. Good.\n\nLet's add aliases in data_loader `_make_match` or in normalize. Maybe better in normalize add a `TEAM_CANONICAL_ALIASES` dict applied in canonical_team_name? Then engine matching teams keys gets correct. But if full name not in alias, query substring still works. We'll add in normalize for centralisation.\n\nBut adding many aliases could slow? no.\n\nLet's add `TEAM_ALIASES` in normalize.py after DISPLAY_ALIASES and apply after canonical calculation.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_efce12a83001vhd0WBiJUdg8PC","sessionID":"ses_103385283ffe30G1XfRK45Z652","messageID":"msg_efce0bb77001jESlR6PnTFY08o"}}
